### Implementation notes

`AnalyticsRepository` now buffers events in an in-memory `Queue<_QueuedEvent>` (max 200, drops oldest on overflow with debugPrint warning). It flushes when:

- buffer reaches `flushBatchSize` (default 20), OR
- `flushInterval` (default 5 s) has elapsed since the first buffered event, OR
- `flush()` is called explicitly, OR
- `onAppLifecyclePaused()` is called (caller-driven hook for app lifecycle).

Drain is serialized via a single `_drainFuture`; concurrent calls return the same future. Each event is POSTed one-at-a-time to `/api/analytics/events` (existing endpoint shape preserved). A `TODO(analytics)` comment marks the future `/api/analytics/events/batch` route.

Retry uses exponential backoff: base 500 ms, doubled per attempt, capped at 5 s, max 3 retries. 5xx and transport exceptions (`SocketException`, `http.ClientException`, `TimeoutException`, generic `catch`) are retried. 4xx is dropped immediately. After max retries, the event is dropped to bound memory. Nothing throws to caller — `track` / `trackEvent` always return a `Future<bool>` where `true` means "queued" (doc-comment updated to call out the semantic change).

Constructor exposes `transport`, `httpClient`, `maxBufferSize`, `flushBatchSize`, `flushInterval`, `maxRetries`, `retryBaseDelay`, `retryMaxDelay`, and a `sleep` injection for tests. `bufferLength` is `@visibleForTesting`. Existing `AnalyticsTransport` interface preserved (so the existing `_FakeAnalyticsTransport` pattern still works), plus the `HttpAnalyticsTransport` default.

